# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository *and* in the working tree on all
# platforms (issue #284).
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with the default `core.autocrlf=true` checks files out
# with CRLF while Prettier is configured with `endOfLine: "lf"` — so `pnpm format:check`
# fails on every file in the repo and `pnpm format` produces an 800-file phantom diff.
# Pinning `eol=lf` keeps the working tree byte-identical to what the linters expect.
#
# Existing Windows clones pick this up on the next checkout; to renormalize one in place:
#   git add --renormalize . && git status

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched by line-ending conversion or textual diffs.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.glb binary
*.gltf binary
*.wasm binary
*.duckdb binary
